course: dictionary
lesson: 13070
title: Fermenting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fermenting is when tiny living things, such as yeast or bacteria, slowly change sugar into gas, acids or alcohol. Context clues can help you spot it. «The bread dough was fermenting in the warm kitchen, and it grew bigger and bigger.» The warm place and the growing dough are clues that something is changing slowly and making gas.
explain: The word can also describe food that is changing on purpose. «The jars of cabbage were fermenting for a week to make sauerkraut.» The cook is choosing to let the food change, so this is fermenting food.
explain: The word can describe feelings and trouble too. «Trouble was fermenting in the class, and nobody was speaking kindly.» Trouble is not in a pot here. It is slowly building up, like a bubble growing. Check your meaning by swapping in "building up slowly" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Fermenting is when tiny living things slowly change sugar into gas, acids or alcohol.
fact: Yeast and bacteria are the tiny living things that do most of the fermenting.
fact: Fermentation makes the bubbles in bread and the sour taste in yogurt and pickles.
fact: «Fermenting» can also mean trouble or anger slowly building up in a group of people.
fact: The verb forms are ferment, ferments, fermented and fermenting; the noun form is fermentation.
exercise: «The bread dough was fermenting in the warm kitchen.» What is happening to the dough? | *Tiny living things are slowly making gas, so it rises | It is being cut into small pieces | It is being frozen solid
exercise: Which food is fermenting on purpose? | *Kimchi left in a jar for several days to sour | A sandwich left on the table by mistake | A cup of cold water from the tap
exercise: «Trouble was fermenting in the class.» What does fermenting mean here? | *Slowly building up | Suddenly gone | Being cooked in a pan | Sweet and sticky
test: What do yeast and bacteria do when they are fermenting? | Turn water into ice | Stop food from changing at all | Make food colder | *Change sugar into gas, acids or alcohol
test: Which word is the noun form of ferment? | fermented | ferments | *fermentation
exam: Which sentence uses fermenting to mean something slowly building up? | *Anger was fermenting in the crowd after the unfair decision | The sugar was fermenting in the cup of tea | The jar of pickles was fermenting on the shelf
